1. In spec.md, FR-004 says priority as mandatory field for ticket creation, 
where as FR 017 says it's not mandatory, as it sets a default value if not provided during creation.

2. In the listTickets API (for listing and filtering), While Listing the tickets for first time, 
it doesn’t send any status from ui.
In API, this parameter is not mandatory; in TicketEntity it is mandatory which is correct. 
But inside service layer in the repo call the query is written in a way where status = null is accepted.
So when after log in user lands on this page, UI sends null which leads to returning null as status = null is passed,  which is wrong.

When no data is returned, API returns 401 unauthorized exception. Which is wrong.
So first the query must be adjusted to handle if no filter criteria is passed in payload.
Secondly if no data found it should give some meaningful message.


3. In ticket creation, the title is mandatory, but in update it was possible to make title blank.
Which is contradictory for create and update
